hosts.tsv, exceptions.tsv, waiting.tsv, SOURCE and coverage.py: the hosts that tracker SDKs send to, graded by
what each host does, the vendors' own apps that keep a host for their own function, and the SDKs still waiting,
compiled by the Datapavan project from the SDKs' own documentation and source code at pinned commits and tags,
Tweasel's tracker wiki (https://trackers.tweasel.org/, published under CC0 1.0) and vendors' own firewall lists,
and dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). Only facts
are recorded, never text from the sources. No row is copied from a blocklist (lists read as leads are named in
SOURCE), and no εxodus data is in these files: the εxodus tracker database (data/exodus, ODbL) and its per-tracker
statistics are read only at run time or by coverage.py, from a copy kept outside this repository. Recorded in
ADR 0052 (W8 part 3a).
